def check_beam(M, Z, f_allow):
    sigma = M / Z
    if sigma <= f_allow:
        status = 'PASS'
    else:
        status = 'FAIL'
    return sigma, status

Test: M = 45 kNm = 45 × 10⁶ N·mm, Z = 500 × 10³ mm³ and f_allow = 275 N/mm². By hand, σ = 45 × 10⁶ / 500 × 10³ = 90 N/mm², which passes. check_beam(45e6, 500e3, 275) should return (90.0, 'PASS'). A second test with f_allow = 80 should return 'FAIL'. Keeping all inputs in N and mm means the stress comes out in N/mm² (MPa).
